Author:     Stephen A Pohl <spohl@mozilla.com>
AuthorDate: Wed Aug 5 19:18:51 2026 +0000
Commit:     spohl@mozilla.com <spohl@mozilla.com>
CommitDate: Wed Aug 5 19:20:58 2026 +0000

    Bug 2045506: Initialize the unread-count dock badge at startup on macOS even when no mail window opens. r=arschmitz,edicharry

    On macOS the application keeps running with no windows open and can be relaunched (for example to apply an update) without a 3pane mail window being shown. The dock unread-count badge is driven by MailNotificationManager, whose init() is only called from the 3pane window (messenger.js loadPostAccountWizard), so in a windowless startup nothing computes or sets the badge until the user opens a window. This is why the badge disappears after an automatic update and reappears when a window is opened.

    Drive MailNotificationManager.init() from MailGlue's window-independent startup path (final-ui-startup) on macOS, and guard init() so it runs only once; the later window-driven call is then a no-op.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310234

diff --git a/mail/components/MailGlue.sys.mjs b/mail/components/MailGlue.sys.mjs
index f030dbbf868..51f8ee061e1 100644
--- a/mail/components/MailGlue.sys.mjs
+++ b/mail/components/MailGlue.sys.mjs
@@ -42,6 +42,8 @@ ChromeUtils.defineESModuleGetters(lazy, {
   LightweightThemeConsumer:
     "resource://gre/modules/LightweightThemeConsumer.sys.mjs",
   MailMigrator: "resource:///modules/MailMigrator.sys.mjs",
+  MailNotificationManager:
+    "resource:///modules/MailNotificationManager.sys.mjs",
   MailServices: "resource:///modules/MailServices.sys.mjs",
   MailUsageTelemetry: "resource:///modules/MailUsageTelemetry.sys.mjs",
   OAuth2Providers: "resource:///modules/OAuth2Providers.sys.mjs",
@@ -656,6 +658,23 @@ MailGlue.prototype = {
     // handle any migration work that has to happen at profile startup
     lazy.MailMigrator.migrateAtProfileStartup();

+    if (
+      AppConstants.platform == "macosx" &&
+      Services.startup.wasSilentlyStarted
+    ) {
+      // A silent start (e.g. relaunching to apply an update) does not open a
+      // mail window, so nothing initializes MailNotificationManager and the
+      // dock unread badge stays blank until the user opens a window. Drive
+      // init() here for that case; it only runs once, so the later
+      // window-driven call from messenger.js is a no-op.
+      //
+      // This is guarded on wasSilentlyStarted (the same flag that keeps the
+      // command line handler from opening a window) rather than run on every
+      // startup, so on a normal windowed startup MailNotificationManager and
+      // the MailNotificationService it pulls in are not loaded here at all.
+      lazy.MailNotificationManager.init();
+    }
+
     if (!Services.prefs.prefHasUserValue(PREF_PDFJS_ISDEFAULT_CACHE_STATE)) {
       lazy.PdfJs.checkIsDefault(this._isNewProfile);
     }
diff --git a/mailnews/base/src/MailNotificationManager.sys.mjs b/mailnews/base/src/MailNotificationManager.sys.mjs
index 4fbf5afa247..2d254204612 100644
--- a/mailnews/base/src/MailNotificationManager.sys.mjs
+++ b/mailnews/base/src/MailNotificationManager.sys.mjs
@@ -130,6 +130,14 @@ export const MailNotificationManager = new (class {
   }

   init() {
+    if (this._initialized) {
+      // init() is called both from the 3pane window (messenger.js) and, on
+      // macOS, from application startup (MailGlue), so that the dock badge is
+      // populated even when no mail window is open. Only run once.
+      return;
+    }
+    this._initialized = true;
+
     this._unreadChatCount = 0;
     this._unreadMailCount = 0;
